spans.s:
ककु॑द् f. peak of a mountain, hump on the shoulders of the
Indian bull;
 head, chief.

ककु॑भ्^1 f. peak, summit;
 region, quarter;
 N. of a metre.
[1] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk on 20160412. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/275.

कक्कोल m. a cert. tree (also ई f.);
 n. (also ˚क n.)
a perfume made of its berries.

क॑क्ष m. hiding-place, recess;
 thicket, weeds;
 f. आ
enclosed court, private apartment;
 m. & f. आ armpit, region of the
girth;
 girdle, cincture;
 balance (mostly f.);
 likeness, similarity;
rivalry, emulation (only f.)

काकपक्ष m. crow's wing;
 a side or temple lock (—˚
also ˚क m).
